{
  "id": "complex-figure-test",
  "term": "Complex Figure Test",
  "definition": "The Complex Figure Test, commonly the Rey-Osterrieth Complex Figure Test, is a neuropsychological assessment of cognitive function in which a person first copies a complicated geometric drawing and later reproduces it from memory. It is used to examine abilities such as visuospatial construction, perceptual organization, executive functioning, and visual memory by judging how accurately and coherently the figure is reproduced.",
